More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (481–490)
481. Improper Validation of API Request Size
API Request Size Validation Vulnerability
APIs fail to limit request sizes, allowing attackers to send extremely large payloads that disrupt services.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
482. Insecure Token Refresh Mechanism
Refresh Token Abuse
Refresh tokens can be reused or stolen, allowing attackers to maintain unauthorized access.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
483. Improper Validation of File Extensions
File Extension Validation Bypass
Applications rely only on file extensions to validate uploads, allowing malicious files.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
484. Insecure Mobile API Endpoints
Mobile API Endpoint Exposure
Mobile application APIs expose sensitive endpoints without authentication.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
485. Improper Validation of Multi-Step Authentication Flow
Multi‑Step Authentication Bypass
Attackers bypass multi-step verification processes during login or transactions.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
486. Improper Handling of API Versioning
Deprecated API Version Exposure
Old API versions remain accessible and contain unpatched vulnerabilities.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
487. Insecure Temporary Upload URLs
Temporary Upload URL Exposure
Temporary upload URLs remain active longer than intended or can be reused.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
488. Improper Security Controls in File Preview Systems
File Preview Execution Vulnerability
File preview services execute malicious content embedded in uploaded files.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
489. Improper Validation of HTTP Cache Headers
Cache Header Information Leakage
Sensitive responses are cached and later accessible to unauthorized users.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
490. Insecure Handling of API Error Messages
Verbose Error Message Exposure
Applications reveal internal server information through detailed error messages.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
